    "details": {
      "alignment": "Lawful Neutral",
      "type": {
        "value": "humanoid",
        "subtype": "Toad"
      },
      "cr": 0.5,
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Chancellor Toadsworth.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 6 → CR 1/2 as a noble. Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Son Who Inherited Everything</strong> — Mushroom Regency (Current Chancellor) / Toadsworth Family Legacy</p><p>Status: Active — under house arrest following Loyalist seizure of Toad Town</p><p>Chancellor Toadsworth is the current head of the Mushroom Regency and the son of Toadsworth the Elder—the man whose journals allegedly confess to enabling Princess Peach's assassination. If those journals are authentic, the Chancellor inherited not just power but COMPLICITY. His father's final written words reportedly state: 'My son inherits what I built. He inherits the secrets with it.' The Chancellor has spent his career maintaining the Regency's official narrative, suppressing investigation leads, and continuing relationships with the Mages' Guild and Iron Legion—both implicated in various aspects of the assassination and its aftermath. He is either a man desperately protecting his father's reputation against terrorist fabrications, or a man actively perpetuating an eighty-five-year cover-up. Captain Toadette's Loyalists recently placed him under house arrest. What they extract from him—through interrogation, coercion, or whatever methods Toadette considers appropriate—may finally answer questions that have haunted the kingdom for generations. Waluigi is not optimistic that the truth will emerge cleanly. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Chancellor's Cane</strong> — “Chancellor Toadsworth is the current head of the Mushroom Regency and the son of Toadsworth the Elder—the man whose journals allegedly confess to enabling Princess Peach's assassination.”</li><li><strong>Official Narrative</strong> — “He inherits the secrets with it.' The Chancellor has spent his career maintaining the Regency's official narrative, suppressing investigation leads, and continuing relationships with the Mages' Guild and Iron”</li><li><strong>The Seals</strong> — “Requests for access to sealed archives are denied.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/chancellor_toadsworth</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/chancellor_toadsworth</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
    },
